  "verbalization": "Skim milk is implicated in the interaction with JAR through a complex network of molecular targets. The evidence suggests that Skim milk interacts with the NF-kappa-B-repressing factor, which is a key regulator of inflammatory and immune responses. This factor is further targeted by 5,4'-Dihydroxy-3,6,3'-trimethoxy-7-prenyloxyflavone and 5,7-Dihydroxy-6-(3-Methylbutanoyl)-8-(3-Methylbut-2-Enyl)-4-Pentylchromen-2-One, both of which are compounds that may have bioactive properties influencing cellular processes. The presence of these targets indicates a potential pathway by which Skim milk could modulate JAR activity, possibly through the activation or inhibition of signaling pathways involving these molecules. The integration of these findings highlights a possible role for Skim milk in regulating JAR through a series of molecular interactions, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated.",
